{
    "purpose": "The native node types, the one source for the internal markdown_core_node_type enum and every per-type table in core/ and elements/. Each class is numbered in list order from 1, so append a type to the end of its class. `kind` names the canonical AST kind (docs/specs/canonical-ast.json) the facade reports, or null for a private type; `ops` names the MARKDOWN_CORE_RECORD_* ops (element.h, markdown_core_record_ops) of the record the node holds, which give its size and its lifecycle, or null for none; `structure` names the MARKDOWN_CORE_ELEMENT_* descriptor that defines the type's block or inline structure, or null. `contain` says what a node of the type may hold as children, or null for nothing: `blocks` and `inlines` hold any type of that class, `members` names the types it holds besides; a `member` type is held only where a type names it, a `root` type never as a child, an `owned` type holds children only when its node's own element declares containment (markdown_core_contain_ops), and a `flat` type never holds its own type. The type string is the lowercased name. Run scripts/tools/generate-node-kinds.mjs after editing.",
